# =============================================================================
# Solver output — NEVER commit these. A single d3plot set or .odb can be
# hundreds of MB and will permanently bloat the repository history. Commit the
# INPUT DECKS, the extracted ASCII results, and the figures.
# =============================================================================

# --- LS-DYNA binary and scratch ---
d3plot*
d3dump*
d3full*
d3hsp
d3kil
dyna.str
runrsf
adptmp
kill_by_pid
mes0*
core.*
*.binout
binout*
scr/

# --- LS-DYNA ASCII output: keep the ones we post-process, ignore the rest ---
# (glstat, matsum, rcforc, bndout, spcforc are DELIBERATELY tracked - see below)
nodout
elout
secforc
sleout
abstat
deforc
jntforc
sbtout
ncforc

# --- Abaqus ---
*.odb
*.lck
*.sta
*.msg
*.dat
*.com
*.prt
*.sim
*.stt
*.mdl
*.res
*.abq
*.pac
*.sel
*.023
*.ipm
*.log
abaqus_v6.env
explicit_dp.env
standard_dp.env

# --- ANSA / META ---
*.ansa_bak
*.metadb
ANSA_TRANSIENT*
META_TRANSIENT*

# --- CAD / mesh intermediates ---
*.stp.bak
*.step.bak
*.prt.*
*.asm.*

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.egg-info/

# --- Editors / OS ---
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*~
*.swp

# =============================================================================
# Explicitly TRACKED despite the patterns above — these are the evidence trail:
#   ls-dyna/**/*.k              input decks
#   abaqus/**/*.inp             input decks
#   results/**/glstat           energy balance
#   results/**/matsum           part energies
#   results/**/rcforc           contact forces
#   results/**/bndout           prescribed-motion reactions
#   results/**/spcforc          constraint reactions
#   results/**/*.json  *.csv    extracted data
#   results/figures/*.png       figures
# Force-add with:  git add -f <path>
# =============================================================================
!ls-dyna/**/*.k
!abaqus/**/*.inp
!results/**/*.json
!results/**/*.csv
!results/figures/*.png
